<title>USA: U.S. August farm prices -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. August farm prices -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA reported average prices farmers received in February, based on prices at mid-month and compared to entire months of January 1997 and February 1996:</p>
<p> (Dlrs/Bu)-- Feb  97   Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p>  All Wheat   3.91     4.03	4.98</p>
<p>	 Corn   2.69     2.69	3.37</p>
<p>   Soybeans   7.37     7.13	7.00</p>
<p>(Dlrs/CWT)--</p>
<p>    Sorghum   4.04     4.04	6.24</p>
<p>   All Hogs  52.60    53.80     46.50</p>
<p>Average Farm Prices, cont.--</p>
<p>		    Feb  97    Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p>(Dlrs/CWT)--</p>
<p>	  Calves   72.60     68.10     60.20</p>
<p>(Cents/Lb) --</p>
<p>	Broilers    39.1	40.4     35.3</p>
<p> Upland Cotton    66.7	67.8     75.7</p>
<p>Note - Current month broiler prices are based on prices received for the entire month, while upland cotton prices are based on sales for the first half of the month.</p>
</text>
